WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.620
Okay.

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:05.899
Let's now go back to the delay of the election
idea that was floated months ago.

00:00:05.899 --> 00:00:10.360
Joe Biden said that he believed Donald Trump
was going to try to create some kind of emergency

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.349
as a pretext to delay the election.

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:16.400
And a whole bunch of people said, oh, Joe
Biden's crazy.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.100
Trump's not going to do that.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.440
And then last week, Donald Trump floated the
idea on Twitter of delaying the election and

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:27.780
has since insisted at every opportunity that
this is going to be a rigged, phony election.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:33.600
A top Democratic congressman in the House
now specifically says that Donald Trump is

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.039
going to use emergency powers to remain in
the White House if he loses the election.

00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:41.829
So this idea is not about delaying the election.

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:44.109
It's about declaring an emergency.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:46.839
If he loses to not vacate the White House.

00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:51.859
Now, I'm talking here about House Majority
Whip Congressman James Clyburn.

00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:57.640
This is probably the strongest reaction from
an actual federal lawmaker so far, saying

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.690
Trump's idea is to put a cloud over the election
and then use some kind of an emergency to

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.900
justify staying in the Oval Office.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:08.710
Here is Congressman Clyburn himself on CNN
Sunday.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:13.610
Do you really think Donald Trump is comparable
to Adolf Hitler?

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:19.880
What I said started at about two and a half,
maybe three years ago at every step of the

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:20.880
unions.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:27.890
But I feel very strongly that this man has
taken on a strong arm tactics, and I feel

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:33.790
very strongly that she is Mussolini who is
Hitler.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:35.590
I said that back then.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:47.050
And I believe that I believe very strongly
this no idea about we want to peacefully transfer

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.050
power.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.230
I don't think he plans to lead the White House.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.710
You don't plan to say it, Alexis.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:02:02.910
I believe that he plans to install himself
in some kind of emergency way to continue

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.720
to hold onto office.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.240
And that's why the American people need to
wake up now.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.930
You know, there are people who are not particularly
pleased with Clyburn, especially because he's

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:16.900
mentioning, you know, Mussolini and Hitler
in the same breath as Trump.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.709
For me, what's lacking is a more detailed
explanation about how exactly Trump plans

00:02:21.709 --> 00:02:22.709
to do it.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:27.519
And so absent a specific plan, I still don't
see this as something that Donald Trump could

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:28.970
actually get away with.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:34.109
But understand that this is a different idea
than delaying the election.

00:02:34.109 --> 00:02:36.209
Delaying the election is what Trump floated
last week.

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:41.269
The idea here is Trump loses, but then uses
some kind of emergency declaration to try

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:42.269
to stay in power.

00:02:42.269 --> 00:02:43.329
So a few different things.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.329
No.

00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:47.760
One, even Republicans are saying all of these
ideas are bogus.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.060
Marco Rubio saying, you know, Trump can suggest
delaying the election, but that's not what's

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.060
going to happen.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:03:01.310
I think that there's actually a point where
the the idea of of debating this is arguably

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.310
the problem.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:08.639
And let me explain to you what I mean when
you bring on experts, politicians, whoever

00:03:08.639 --> 00:03:12.900
to argue about can Trump delay the election?

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.019
Could he use an emergency to stay in power
or whatever?

00:03:17.019 --> 00:03:20.730
You are legitimizing the idea of this as a
concept.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:27.980
And what I mean by that is the real newsworthiness
of this story is the wildly authoritarian,

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:31.239
completely unhinged idea of delaying the election.

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:35.200
That's what needs to be reported on when you
bring in a member of Congress or a legal expert

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:41.319
and say, could Trump do this or how could
Trump do this, or is Trump doing this justified?

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:44.519
You are creating the notion that there's something
to debate here.

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:48.159
I do a bit of a different type of show than
what you see on corporate media.

00:03:48.159 --> 00:03:51.609
So I've pointed out Trump can't really do
the states run their own elections.

00:03:51.609 --> 00:03:55.489
You need at the federal level some kind of
decree from the House and Senate, which you're

00:03:55.489 --> 00:03:56.970
not going to get.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:03.739
But the focus of this story needs to be on
corporate media that Donald Trump is alluding

00:04:03.739 --> 00:04:06.959
to something completely authoritarian and
dictatorial.

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:13.659
It is the idea of something that despot's
do and normalizing this idea of a delay or

00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:15.889
staying in power.

00:04:15.889 --> 00:04:21.840
Is almost saying it could be justified if
there is the debate as to whether Trump would

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.590
have the legal authority to do this.

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:32.150
It validates what should be a completely immediately
dismissed authoritarian idea.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:35.650
That's my concern about some of these types
of segments.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.639
So I'm curious to hear from you about that.

00:04:37.639 --> 00:04:37.819
Let me know what you think.

